.TH NSS-LOOKUP 1 "2026-10-13" "SASD Freeware" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
nss-lookup \- targeted libc/NSS user and group lookup
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B nss-lookup
.RB ( --user " NAME | " --uid " N | " --group " NAME | " --gid " N) [" --null ]
.br
.B nss-lookup
.RB [ --help | --version ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Resolve one user or group from the host's configured libc name service.
Does not enumerate NSS, change identities, or report which backend answered.
A successful result does not prove LDAP/NIS enumeration completeness.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI --user " NAME"
Lookup user by name.
.TP
.BI --uid " N"
Lookup user by decimal UID.
.TP
.BI --group " NAME"
Lookup group by name.
.TP
.BI --gid " N"
Lookup group by decimal GID.
.TP
.B --null
Seven raw NUL-separated TYPE, NAME, UID, GID, HOME, SHELL, MEMBERS fields.
.TP
.B --help
Display help.
.TP
.B --version
Display version.
.SH OUTPUT
Human output is tab-delimited with control characters escaped.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 found; 1 not found (may include backend failure not distinguished by libc); 2 usage error.
.SH SEE ALSO
getpwnam(3), getgrnam(3), nsswitch.conf(5)
